completed_at: "2026-09-18T14:04:17.208Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The --profile output reports end-to-end invocation latency measured from process entry to output flush, and any narrower spans it also reports are labelled with what they cover so the total and its parts are distinguishable. The reported total agrees with externally measured wall clock within a stated tolerance for every command family, asserted by a regression test rather than by inspection. --profile is documented with its measured span and its output shape. Any latency budget or ratchet in this repository consumes the end-to-end figure."
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Emit one opt-in stderr invocation total from runtime startup through natural output drain, with explicitly scoped legacy handler spans."
expected_result: "Profiling reflects executable lifetime across help, version, queries, mutations, and refusals while preserving stdout and external performance budgets."
actual_result: Real Node and Bun timing agrees with external wall clocks; process-family and lifecycle regressions pass; transport budgets and exact full coverage pass.
