comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T10:29:58.742Z","harness:opencode","Fresh evidence 2026-07-26 (audit plan pm-t9e3bc): wall-clock re-measured on live tracker now at 2,066 items, dist 2026.7.26, Node 25.9.0 — pm context --limit 5: 1132/1224/1306ms across runs; pm search audit --limit 5: 1005/1105/1151ms; pm list-open --limit 5: 743/919ms; pm get pm-doxj --depth brief: 635/875ms; pm --version: 57ms; pm contracts --flags-only: 643ms. The ~600-800ms constant un-instrumented floor this item documents persists unchanged on current main; experienced read latency at the 2k-item dogfood scale remains ~1s+ for context/search, so the pm-801d read index relieves daily agent-perceived latency long before the 100k-item scale framing."
  "2026-08-04T09:18:09.684Z","harness:codex","Fresh latency evidence 2026-08-04: the transport-floor gate first failed pm next at best 464ms against 440ms, then passed unchanged on immediate rerun. The separate 10k-item CLI+SDK scale gate passed all 14 command/transport targets: CLI p95 341-776ms, SDK p95 12-264ms, all under 1s and token budgets. The user-visible fixed process/bootstrap floor and noisy single-run threshold remain distinct from scale-algorithm health."
  "2026-09-18T13:04:17.017Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: process-level timing from runtime startup through drained output, preserving the existing handler diagnostics with an explicit span label. Existing transport and scale gates already measure external process wall time; retain those authoritative budgets. All-status history reviewed, including completed pm-yse5dt; no duplicate item created."
  "2026-09-18T13:10:53.233Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: both new integration regressions failed against the original implementation. Provenance still reported zero successes after a real SDK mutation with a recovered session probe; executable profiling emitted no invocation total for version/help. Tests use isolated trackers and real filesystem/process boundaries."
  "2026-09-18T13:21:41.269Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance: ten isolated real CLI commands (init/create/claim/update/comments/close/release/get/validate/full health) each emitted exactly one invocation total. External wall times were 608-978 ms under concurrent validation load; process totals were 560-896 ms. Unprofiled JSON remained valid. Full typecheck, eslint, duplicate gates, secret scan, and docs/skills checks passed. Packed npm/npx/bunx smoke passed with nine packages."
  "2026-09-18T13:36:16.521Z","harness:codex","Cross-runtime timing acceptance: direct Node and Bun version/help invocations emitted exactly one total each, below externally measured wall time. Fresh packed first-run acceptance passed the README workflow, merge-history behavior, MCP handshake, real detached telemetry completion, and physical queue drain."
  "2026-09-18T13:54:25.068Z","harness:codex","Final repository gate evidence before hosted review: pnpm quality:static passed the complete lint/duplicates/build/contracts/static assurance/package boundaries/replication/grammar/flag parity/refusal/token/MCP/tracker-context/SDK surface/SDK import-cost/transport/graph/record-integrity chain. Sequential temporary package-first dogfood passed 89 commands, including an authored TypeScript package, SDK import, extension workflows, and a real linked test. Linked profiling tests passed."
  "2026-09-18T14:04:14.502Z","harness:codex","Final local validation passed: 708 files / 9006 tests; exact coverage 64834/64834 statements, 49486/49486 branches, 13456/13456 functions, 62056/62056 lines. No threshold reductions or coverage exclusions were introduced. Full static-quality chain, linked tests, typecheck, 89-command dogfood, packed npm/npx/bunx, installed first-run/MCP/telemetry, docs, and security checks passed. Implementation complete; hosted review and merge are the remaining delivery steps."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T13:54:50.535Z","harness:codex","Compatibility: the final executable receipt is opt-in and stderr-only. Existing handler records and external process-wall performance budgets retain their formats and thresholds; SDK hosts own their own lifetime. Normal process drain is required, so forced termination may have no final receipt."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-18T13:26:15.232Z","harness:codex","Use runtime uptime at natural process drain for executable timing, and retain external wall-clock performance budgets. Measure performance without concurrent coverage or static-analysis load; keep handler spans explicitly scoped."
